{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008748-practical-uses-of-entropy-and-powerplay","id":1008748,"title":"Practical uses of entropy and powerplay","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-26T19:25:12-08:00","id":1008748,"title":"Practical uses of entropy and powerplay","content":"So I kinda get that entropy shifts luck and probability giving u bonus or penalties. I decided to allow in real game for an entropy mage to gain a -1 to -3 difficulty discount on the actions he chooses, give enemies a +1 to +3 penalty on all their actions difficulties , being able to have bonus dices or steal dices from their enemies pools, and even/ starting at entropy 3,/ add automatic successes or subtract successes from a personal dice roll or an enemy roll.<br /> <br /> Now my question is - and keep in mind that it's one of the questions I would not want to ask but I have to-<br /> CAN ENTROPY AFFECT ARETE ROLLS?<br /> <br /> I couldn't find the answer to my doubt anywhere so I thought I'd ask.<br /> This might be the most broken power of entropy.in the game so it's kind of a big deal.<br /> Don't know if u guys followed but it's the reason why in mage the awakening Acanthus mages are simply broken and given some turn of preparation they could overpower any mage or magic with massive dice pools on casting spells.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this? If entropy controls the destiny probability and luck of any event or gesture, why shouldn't it be able to diminish the difficulty for spellcasting ? Or give more bonus to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T23:36:00-08:00","id":1008834,"title":"","content":"I would say No. Sphere magick generally shouldn't be used to affect the difficulty of other Sphere magick. That seems a recipe for disaster, and would make Entropy way too overpowered.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind also that, assuming Entropy can indeed raise or lower mundane rolls, other Spheres have a similar ability where appropriate. M20 has an entire sidebar devoted to listing various Effects - mostly first or second level spells - that can provide such basic bonuses to rolls. Forces can intensify and direct kinetic energy, Life gives bonus dice to physical actions through buffed Attributes, etc. So Entropy is hardly unique in this regard, and one might logically assume that there are some actions where manipulation of luck wouldn't help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-27-2016, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:25:28-08:00","id":1008856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008748-practical-uses-of-entropy-and-powerplay?p=1008834#post1008834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Entropy is hardly unique in this regard, and one might logically assume that there are some actions where manipulation of luck wouldn't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Magick being one of them, I'd say.<br /> The right way of doing this is to include Entropy in the effect or rote that you are casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-27-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:27:41-08:00","id":1008919,"title":"","content":"At most I would allow an effect to make an ability roll easier that in turn makes an arete roll easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T08:50:52-08:00","id":1008929,"title":"","content":"I would say yes, it is however a bit difficult. <br /> <br /> I would allow players to start messing with enemies foci starting at Entropy 3. The Hermetic is waving his phallic symbol at you? Well it'd be a shame if it broke at an inopportune moment. Mechanically I would make the subject of such a curse roll an Attribute + Ability roll the difficulty of which would be Base difficulty of the Spell + successes (max +3). So in our example let's say that said Hermetic was the subject of a 4 success Entropy 3 curse. He wanted to Blast you with a gout of conjured fire (Vulgar Magic, let's assume without witnesses), because of the curse he has to roll Dexterity + Esoterica. Base difficulty of the spell is 7 (Forces 3, Prime 2), +3 because of 4 successes on the curse (not +4 because +3 is the maximum modifier). So he has to succeed on a difficulty 10 Dex + Esoterica roll (thank god for willpower <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). If he succeeds he rolls his Arete for the spell as normal, if he fails the difficulty modifier of the curse applies to his Arete roll (again maximum +3) and if he botches... well his spell botches. If your wand breaks while you channel the forces of fire through it it may just explode in your face.<br /> <br /> Of course this only works for Foci which could be affected with an Entropy 3 effect. If the hermetic simply used an enochian invocation to channel the power the player would have to resort to Entropy 4 to achieve a similar effect (not targeting the words themselves, that would require Entropy 5, but rather the body of the caster, making him mispronounce at an inopportune moment). Mages superceeding foci cannot really be affected with these effects.<br /> <br /> Once you reach Entropy 5... oh boy. Here is where the fun starts. An Entropy 5 effect could potentially muddy the whole concept of magic for the subject, forcing intelligence rolls to even figure out how to work his will. Even superceeding foci doesn't protect you from a master of Entropy! Given enough successes such a spell could make it downright impossible for the subject to work magic (a Mind 4 effect could achieve similar results btw, just as a Mind 3 effect could emulate the effects Entropy 4 achieved), though such an effect would probably need to at least outscore the enemies willpower rating in successes and would allmost certainly be of temporary nature.<br /> <br /> Now the next part is a bit homeruley I suppose. Entropy 5 has been stated to touch upon the subjects of Mind, Spirit, Time and Space, I personally see no reason why it should be able to affect magic itself (sort of the domain of prime) similarily. So I'd allow an Entropy 5 effect to play with the forces of magic directly, adding for example virtual 1s to an enemies arete roll or perhaps even turning failures into botches. I'd proably allow prime at higher levels to do similar stuff though, overloading the enemies magic and making it more likely to explode into their faces... probably just Prime 3 or 4 really, no idea atm where I would place that exactly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T12:27:00-08:00","id":1009002,"title":"","content":"I would not allow Entropy Effects to affect Arete rolls directly. Mages are willworkers so their ability to perform True Magick is concious and there is nothing random about that. However, it is possible to affect rituals with entropy by affecting ability rolls or using the entropy effects to impact the scene of the casting. You could for exemple use Entropy effects to disturb your target and make him miss his magick (losing focus in a ritual is close to a botch). I would say that you can impact a spell by acting indirectly on the Mage, but not by affecting his arete roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8572-nicotheduck","name":"NicoTheDuck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T02:57:18-08:00","id":1010988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NicoTheDuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1008748-practical-uses-of-entropy-and-powerplay?p=1009002#post1009002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not allow Entropy Effects to affect Arete rolls directly. Mages are willworkers so their ability to perform True Magick is concious and there is nothing random about that. However, it is possible to affect rituals with entropy by affecting ability rolls or using the entropy effects to impact the scene of the casting. You could for exemple use Entropy effects to disturb your target and make him miss his magick (losing focus in a ritual is close to a botch). I would say that you can impact a spell by acting indirectly on the Mage, but not by affecting his arete roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too would not want to allow Entropy to provide *direct* difficulty reductions on Arete rolls, but for balance reasons.<br /> <br /> However, I disagree with your stance of the nature of conscious thought/action. Causality demands that mental events must be influenced by the past and present events; some of such influences are quite random! In fact, Entropy explicitly says that it can affect even thoughts at level 5 (though affecting a living body at E4 or a mechanical body of an uploaded mage at E3 might be sufficient too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12622,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","user":"vicky_molokh","date":". 12-02-2016, 06:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T03:36:33-08:00","id":1010993,"title":"","content":"Entropy *can* affect Arete rolls, in the way that Entropy, as mentioned by NicoTheDuck in regards to Rituals, and Nonsense in regards to general abilities, can affect the rolls that are *required* to pull off the Arete roll afterwards.<br /> <br /> Any Instrument that boils down to an ability-based pre-Arete roll can be made easier and/or Influenced by a previous application of Entropy Magick - and this is important: It's not just Entropy Magick that can do this!<br /> <br /> For example using Life Magick to increase your Dexterity, which you <i>then</i> use in your dex+performance ability roll for, say, an Instrument of Dance will increase the potential successes for the dancing, and <i>in consequence</i> can make the Arete roll that uses it as an instrument easier.<br /> <br /> Good results on ability rolls of Instruments like that making Arete rolls easier is even described in M20. Page 562, '<i>Abilities enhancing an Effect</i>'.<br /> It is the advantage of ability-based Instruments that require you to make a roll before the Arete-roll. Instruments that don't require a roll have the disadvantage that they can't make the Arete roll easier..but they don't require a roll. Their advantage is that they thus can't make it harder, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-02-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}